
<%
  node_count = local_assigns[:node_count]
  edge_count = local_assigns[:edge_count]
  connected_node_count = local_assigns[:connected_node_count]
  isolated_node_count = local_assigns[:isolated_node_count]
%>

<section class="overflow-hidden rounded-[28px] border-2 border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-lg shadow-slate-100/40"
         aria-labelledby="metric-explainer-title">
  <header class="border-b-2 border-slate-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-50 via-white to-orange-50/40 p-5 sm:p-7">
    <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-600">Reference guide</p>
    <h2 id="metric-explainer-title" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl">
      What do the numbers mean?
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
      Metrics are useful when their definitions and scope are clear. Use this guide to avoid over-interpreting
      graph statistics or treating missing values as zero.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 p-5 sm:p-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-orange-100 bg-orange-50/40 p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-900">Entities</h3>
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">🌍</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tabular-nums text-orange-800">
        <%= node_count.nil? ? "—" : number_with_delimiter(node_count) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Distinct entity records included in the current response. This may differ from the total number
        of records stored in the database.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-sky-100 bg-sky-50/40 p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-900">Relationships</h3>
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">🔗</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tabular-nums text-sky-800">
        <%= edge_count.nil? ? "—" : number_with_delimiter(edge_count) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Relationship records represented by edges in the response. Depending on your data model,
        edges may be directed, typed, or supported by additional evidence.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/40 p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-900">Connected entities</h3>
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">🕸️</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tabular-nums text-emerald-800">
        <%= connected_node_count.nil? ? "—" : number_with_delimiter(connected_node_count) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Entities that the backend reports as having at least one relevant connection.
        Whether hidden or filtered edges count depends on the service implementation.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-violet-100 bg-violet-50/40 p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-900">Isolated entities</h3>
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black tabular-nums text-violet-800">
        <%= isolated_node_count.nil? ? "—" : number_with_delimiter(isolated_node_count) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Entities reported without a visible connection in the relevant graph scope.
        Isolation alone does not indicate a data-quality problem.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="border-t-2 border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-900">A practical rule</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-slate-700">
      If a value is shown as an em dash, the value was not supplied. Do not substitute zero unless
      the service explicitly reports zero. Always consider graph scope, filters, and response limits
      when comparing snapshots.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>